bsnes-jg-player — the reusable browser player integration for bsnes-jg, using WebAssembly.

This project builds and redistributes the following under the GNU GPL v3:

  bsnes-jg 2.1.0
    A cycle-accurate Super Famicom / SNES emulator; fork of bsnes v115.
    Upstream:        https://gitlab.com/jgemu/bsnes   (the "Jolly Good" fork)
    bsnes original:  Near (byuu) et al.
    License:         GNU General Public License, version 3 (see LICENSE)
    This is the exact version (sha256-pinned) the llvm-mos-65816 differential
    gate trusts; build.sh compiles it to WebAssembly unmodified except for an
    added Emscripten-fiber backend for its bundled libco (web/src/libco_*.c).

The core is driven by our own minimal Jolly-Good-API frontend (web/src/main.cpp)
rendering to a <canvas> — no libretro, no EmulatorJS. The bsnes-jg tarball bundles
its dependencies, which are compiled into the wasm build and carry their own
licenses: libsamplerate (BSD-2-Clause), libco (ISC), SameBoy/gb, snes_spc, byuuML.

Bundled ROMs (web/roms/*.sfc) are homebrew demos compiled by the llvm-mos-65816
toolchain (https://github.com/wbniv/llvm-mos-65816) from that project's own
example sources — included here so the page runs out of the box.

The build scripts, loader page, and documentation original to this repository are
licensed GPLv3 to match the core they ship.
